{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothAuxiliaryPolynomial","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothAuxiliaryPolynomial","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothGammaProducer"],"declarations":44,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.nsmul_fintypeCard_idxWeight_lt_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.nsmul_fintypeCard_idxWeight_lt_witness","kind":"theorem","line":650,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L650-L659","doc":"**Non-vacuity, and the threshold really does move with the degree.**  At `ε = 1/2` and\n`m = 5` the multiplicity-`4` system is still underdetermined (`4 < 4·(1/4)·5 = 5`), but the\nmultiplicity-`5` one is not covered — `5 < 5` is false.  So `deg α` is not decoration: the same\n`m` that suffices for a degree-4 `α` fails to be justified for a degree-5 one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.nsmul_fintypeCard_idxWeight_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.nsmul_fintypeCard_idxWeight_lt","kind":"theorem","line":639,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L639-L648","doc":"**The form Siegel over `ℤ` consumes.**  `deg α · #conditions < #unknowns`, with the counts as\n`Fintype.card`s of the subtypes the linear system is indexed by. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.nsmul_card_idxWeight_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.nsmul_card_idxWeight_lt","kind":"theorem","line":630,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L630-L637","doc":"The multi-index form of `nsmul_card_lt_card_idxBox_of_eps`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.fintypeCard_idxWeight_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.fintypeCard_idxWeight_lt","kind":"theorem","line":619,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L619-L628","doc":"**`p < q`, exactly as `Int.Matrix.exists_ne_zero_int_vec_norm_le` asks for it** — the\nequations indexed by a subtype, the unknowns by another, and `Fintype.card` between them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_idxWeight_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_idxWeight_lt","kind":"theorem","line":609,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L609-L617","doc":"**The vanishing conditions are fewer than the coefficients**, in the arc's own `idxWeight`\nlanguage: at index threshold `m(½ − ε)`, as soon as `m > 1/(4ε²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_filter_idxBoxF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_filter_idxBoxF","kind":"theorem","line":593,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L593-L607","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mem_idxBoxF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mem_idxBoxF","kind":"theorem","line":588,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L588-L591","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_idxBoxF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_idxBoxF","kind":"theorem","line":585,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L585-L586","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.idxBoxF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.idxBoxF","kind":"def","line":581,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L581-L583","doc":"The box of multi-indices, carried onto `Finsupp`s — the form `index` speaks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.centredWeight_equivFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.centredWeight_equivFun","kind":"theorem","line":574,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L574-L579","doc":"**The two weights differ by the mean.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.idxWeight_eq_sum_univ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.idxWeight_eq_sum_univ","kind":"theorem","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L564-L572","doc":"**`idxWeight`, as a sum over all coordinates.**  `idxWeight` sums over the support; on a\nfinite index type the missing terms are `0/d = 0`, so the two agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_translateMatrix_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_translateMatrix_le","kind":"theorem","line":530,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L530-L545","doc":"**The integer instance.**  `|binom(n,i)·α^{n−i}| ≤ (2B)^{|n|}` for integer `α` bounded by `B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.seminorm_translateMatrix_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.seminorm_translateMatrix_le","kind":"theorem","line":467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L467-L528","doc":"**The translate matrix is small.**  `f (binom(n,i)·α^{n−i}) ≤ (2B)^{|n|}` where `|n|` is the\ntotal degree and `B` bounds `f ∘ α` — proved by peeling one variable occurrence at a time, so the\nmultivariate binomial closed form is never needed.\n\nThe `2` is the two terms of `X_j + C α_j`; the `B` is the constant one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.mul_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.mul_le","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L465-L465","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.add_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.add_le","kind":"theorem","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L464-L464","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.one_le","kind":"theorem","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L463-L463","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.map_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.map_zero","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L462-L462","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L461-L461","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L460-L460","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm","kind":"structure","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L458-L465","doc":"A submultiplicative seminorm — the only structure the translate-matrix bound needs.\n`house` is one (`house_nonneg`, `house_sum_le_sum_house`, `house_mul_le`); so is `|·|` on `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_idxBox_five_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_idxBox_five_witness","kind":"theorem","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L419-L422","doc":"The box in the witness above really does have `2⁵ = 32` points, so the strict inequality is\nnot `0 < 0`.  ⚠ This part *is* checked; the count of the filtered set is not — see above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_lt_card_idxBox_of_eps_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_lt_card_idxBox_of_eps_witness","kind":"theorem","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L401-L417","doc":"**Non-vacuity of the `ε` form**, at `ε = ¼`, `m = 5`, `r ≡ 1`: the threshold `1 < 4ε²m`\nreads `1 < 5/4`.\n\nThe box has `2⁵ = 32` points (`card_idxBox_five_witness`, checked).  The filtered set is the\nmulti-indices with `∑ x_h ≤ 1`, since `centredWeight x = ∑ x_h − 5/2` and the threshold is\n`−5/4`; that is **six** of them, and the strict inequality is not a near miss.\n\n⚠ The `6` is a hand count, **not** checked by the build: `decide` gets stuck on this goal because\nthe filter's `Decidable` instance does not reduce (it goes through `Rat.instDecidableLe` and then\n`Finset.filter` over `Fintype.piFinset` and stalls).  Recorded rather than quietly asserted —\na number in a docstring that the build has no opinion about is what corrections 17 and 24 in\nthis arc were both about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.nsmul_card_lt_card_idxBox_of_eps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.nsmul_card_lt_card_idxBox_of_eps","kind":"theorem","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L389-L399","doc":"**`deg α` in the counting, at Roth's threshold.**  The system with multiplicity `n` is\nunderdetermined as soon as `n < 4ε²m` — so \"take `m` large\" becomes `m > n/(4ε²)`, and the degree\nof `α` sets how large.  At `n = 1` this is `card_lt_card_idxBox_of_eps`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.nsmul_card_lt_card_idxBox","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.nsmul_card_lt_card_idxBox","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L365-L387","doc":"**The counting condition with a multiplicity — `deg α · #conditions < #unknowns`.**\n\nThe classical form.  Each `K`-linear vanishing condition is `deg α` conditions over `ℚ`, so a\n`ℤ`-coefficient auxiliary polynomial needs the *weighted* count to stay under the number of\nunknowns.  `card_lt_card_idxBox` is this at `n = 1`, which is what Mathlib's number-field Siegel\nlemma needs and what an auxiliary polynomial over `𝓞 K` would use — but that polynomial cannot\nfeed Roth's Lemma, which is stated over `ℤ`.  See the ⚠⚠ in the header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_lt_card_idxBox_of_eps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_lt_card_idxBox_of_eps","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L351-L363","doc":"**Where `m` gets chosen.**  For an index threshold `m(½ − ε)` — i.e. `centredWeight ≤ −εm` —\nthe system is underdetermined as soon as `m > 1/(4ε²)`.\n\nThis is Roth's \"take `m` sufficiently large\", with the bound made explicit, and it is the whole\npurpose of the variance computation: the threshold scales with `m` while the standard deviation\nscales with `√m`, so the fraction below it goes to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_lt_card_idxBox","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_lt_card_idxBox","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L333-L349","doc":"**The system is underdetermined.**  Fewer vanishing conditions than coefficients, as soon\nas `m < 4λ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_idxBox_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_idxBox_pos","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L329-L331","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_idxBox_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_idxBox_witness","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L324-L326","doc":"…and the box in that witness really does have two elements, so the count is not `0 ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_centredWeight_le_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_centredWeight_le_witness","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L314-L322","doc":"**Non-vacuity of the counting**, at `m = 1`, `r = 1`, `λ = 1/2`.  The box is `{0, 1}`, the\ncentred weights are `∓1/2`, so exactly one index sits at or below `−1/2` and the bound reads\n`1 · ¼ ≤ ¼ · 2` — tight to within a factor `2`, which is the `r = 1` end of `(r+2)/(12r) ≤ ¼`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_centredWeight_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_centredWeight_le","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L286-L312","doc":"**Chebyshev, for the Roth index distribution.**  The multi-indices of weight at least `λ`\nbelow the mean `m/2` are a fraction at most `m/(4λ²)` of the box.\n\n⚠ The `m` in the numerator is the whole point.  Cauchy–Schwarz on `(∑ u_h)² ≤ m ∑ u_h²` would\ngive `m²/(4λ²)`, and with Roth's `λ = εm` that reads `1/(4ε²)` — a constant, with no `m` left to\ngrow.  The variance being `O(m)` rather than `O(m²)` is exactly what lets `m` be chosen large\nenough to beat the degree of `α`, so the vanishing cross terms are load-bearing and not a\ntidiness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_centredWeight_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_centredWeight_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L255-L284","doc":"**Variance at most `m/4`.**  Each coordinate contributes `(r+2)/(12r) ≤ 1/4`, with equality\nat `r = 1`; the true asymptote is `1/12`, and `1/4` is the price of allowing `r = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_centredWeight_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_centredWeight_sq","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L226-L253","doc":"**The second moment, exactly.**  The cross terms are gone; only the `m` diagonal terms\nsurvive, each a one-coordinate second moment times the size of the other coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_idxBox","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_idxBox","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L222-L224","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.centredWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.centredWeight","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L218-L220","doc":"The **centred** Roth weight: `∑ x_h/r_h − m/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.idxBox","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.idxBox","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L214-L216","doc":"The box of multi-indices bounded by `r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_piFinset_pair_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_piFinset_pair_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L188-L212","doc":"**The cross terms vanish.**  Independence of the coordinates, in the only form the variance\ncomputation needs: if one factor has zero marginal sum, the pair sum is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_piFinset_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_piFinset_single","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L168-L186","doc":"**A single-coordinate marginal over a product box.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_centred_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_centred_sq","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L153-L167","doc":"**Second moment, one coordinate.**  `(r+1)(r+2)/(12r)` — at `r = 1` and `r = 2` it is `1/2`\nboth times, which is the arithmetic check worth doing by hand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_centred_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_centred_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L140-L151","doc":"**First moment, one coordinate: zero.**  This is what kills the cross terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_range_sq_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_range_sq_cast","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L134-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_range_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_range_cast","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L128-L132","doc":"Gauss, over `ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coeff_translate_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coeff_translate_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L112-L125","doc":"**The equations are linear in `P`'s coefficients**, with `translateMatrix` as the matrix.\nThis is the input Siegel's lemma takes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.translateMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.translateMatrix","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L106-L110","doc":"**The translate matrix.**  The entry at `(i, n)` is the coefficient of `x^i` in the\ntranslate of the bare monomial `x^n` — Roth's `binom(n,i)·α^{n−i}`, defined without needing the\nclosed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.le_index_iff_coeff_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.le_index_iff_coeff_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryPolynomial.lean#L88-L104","doc":"**The index condition, as equations.**  `c ≤ index d α P` says exactly that every\ntranslate-coefficient of weight below `c` vanishes — a finite set of linear conditions on `P`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}